.TH REVERBLABR-CTL 1 2026-09-28 "Reverblabr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reverblabr\-ctl \- run and change Reverblabr sessions from a terminal or a script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reverblabr\-ctl
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-activate ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reverblabr\-ctl
asks Reverblabr's engine to start and stop sessions, split their
recordings, turn their Input Switches, change their blocks' settings and
list and fire their timers.
It is a client of the engine's public D-Bus API on the session bus, and
the engine does the work: a session changed here changes in every open
Reverblabr window at the same time.
.PP
The first call starts the engine if it is installed and not running.
.PP
A session is named by its name or its id, and a block by its name or its
id. A name that matches nothing exactly may match ignoring case; a name
that two sessions or two blocks share is refused, with their ids, rather
than guessed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
The sessions' names, one a line.
.TP
.BR status " [\fIsession\fR]"
Every session and its state, or one session's: running, stopped, closed
(on disk, not open), or could not run.
.TP
.BI start " session"
Runs a session, opening it first if it is only on disk. A session that
already runs is left as it is.
.TP
.BI stop " session"
Stops a session. A session that does not run is left as it is.
.TP
.BR split " \fIsession\fR [\fIrecorder\fR]"
Ends the file every Recorder of a running session is writing, or the
named Recorder's, and starts the next with no gap.
.TP
.BR switch " \fIsession\fR [\fIswitch\fR] " A | B
Turns an Input Switch to input A or B. The switch may be left out when the
session has only one.
.TP
.BI set " session block setting value"
Changes one setting of a block, as one step the window can undo. The value
is checked against the setting: a number in its range, true or false (also
on, off, yes, no, 1, 0), or one of its choices. A session only on disk is
opened for the change and closed again, and the change is saved.
.TP
.BR "timers list" " [\fIsession\fR]"
Every session's timers, or one session's, a line each: when it runs, for
how long, when it next starts its session, and its id in brackets.
Timers are made in the Schedule tab.
.TP
.BR timer\-fire " [\fB\-\-scheduled\fR] \fItimer\fR"
Does now what the timer does when its time comes: opens its session if it
is only on disk, starts it, and has the engine stop it once the timer's
duration is over. A session already running is left as it is, and the
answer says so. The systemd user timer Reverblabr writes for each timer
that is on runs this with \fB\-\-scheduled\fR, which has a fire more than
two minutes after the timer's time, as after the computer slept, refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Prints the answer, or the failure, as one line of JSON on standard output.
It is the same in every language, and its fields are only ever added to.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
How long to wait for the engine's answer. The default is 10.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-activate
Only asks an engine that is already running, and never starts one.
.TP
.B \-\-scheduled
For \fBtimer\-fire\fR only: the fire is the timer's own, from its systemd
unit, and is refused when it comes too late.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Prints the commands.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the version.
.TP
.B \-\-
Ends the options, for a name that begins with a dash.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done, or nothing to do (a session already running, or already stopped).
.TP
.B 1
The engine refused, with an error code: a session could not start, a
change was refused, a recording could not be split.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong: an unknown command or option, a missing
argument, or a value the setting cannot take.
.TP
.B 3
No session, block, setting or timer by that name, or more than one.
.TP
.B 4
No engine to ask: no session bus, or the engine is not installed, would
not start, or with \fB\-\-no\-activate\fR is not running.
.TP
.B 5
The engine did not answer in time.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus to reach the engine on.
.TP
.BR LANGUAGE ", " LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
The language of the messages. The \fB\-\-json\fR output is never
translated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
reverblabr\-ctl start "Evening radio"
reverblabr\-ctl status \-\-json | jq \-r '.sessions[] | select(.state == "running") | .name'
reverblabr\-ctl switch "Evening radio" B
reverblabr\-ctl set "Evening radio" Voice gain 0.5
reverblabr\-ctl split "Evening radio"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR busctl (1)
.PP
The JSON each command prints: docs/ctl.md in Reverblabr's source. The D-Bus
API itself: docs/dbus-api.md.
